      "text": "To find the distance between the foci of the ellipse, we first need to identify the key parameters of the ellipse from the given diagram. The ellipse is centered at \\((1,1)\\) with a semi-major axis \\(a\\) and a semi-minor axis \\(b\\).\n\nFrom the diagram, we can see that:\n- The length of the semi-major axis \\(a\\) is 6.\n- The length of the semi-minor axis \\(b\\) is 2.\n\nThe distance between the foci of an ellipse is given by \\(2c\\), where \\(c\\) is calculated using the relationship:\n\\[ c = \\sqrt{a^2 - b^2} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):\n\\[ c = \\sqrt{6^2 - 2^2} = \\sqrt{36 - 4} = \\sqrt{32} = 4\\sqrt{2} \\]\n\nTherefore, the distance between the foci is:\n\\[ 2c = 2 \\times 4\\sqrt{2} = 8\\sqrt{2} \\]\n\nSo, the distance between the foci is:\n\\[ \\boxed{8\\sqrt{2}} \\]",
